      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{6161a61a2c0de966b4e43486|full_name} I see, I thought \"2000 operations\" would mean math operations in the parameter behaviors section. 512 is a lot more restrictive than I imagined, especially considering tracking key variables AND numeric constants count against the instruction limit.\n\nIs there any wiggle room on this before it reaches public release? I was hoping FT artists would be able to replace their entire animators with math, which would be great for performance, but under these restrictions only super straightforward setups actually fit under the instruction limit.",
